<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert, Duke of Prussia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1490">1490</a>–<a href="/years/1568">1568</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Albert of Prussia, Albrecht of Brandenburg-Ansbach, Albert of Brandenburg-Ansbach, Albrecht of Prussia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, a Hohenzollern of the Ansbach line, was the last Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in Prussia. In 1525, advised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a>, he converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> and secularised the Order's state as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a>, the first Protestant state. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Samland and Pomesania handed him their secular powers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-duke-of-prussia.jpg" alt="Albert, Duke of Prussia" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Bildnis_des_Markgrafen_Albrecht_von_Brandenburg-Ansbach_(Herzog_Anton_Ulrich-Museum).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
